[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114284,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nasopalatine duct cyst (NDC) is a developmental non-odontogenic cyst arising in the incisive canal.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114285,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114286,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DA05.1 Developmental non-odontogenic cysts of oral region</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114287,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> incisive canal cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114288,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114289,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>NDCs present in the midline of the anterior hard palate.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114290,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most NDCs present as sessile swellings posterior to the maxillary incisors, or they may be entirely asymptomatic. More deeply sited cysts present as a swelling on the labial alveolus or bulging into the nasal floor {23285406; 29248496}. Rarely, an NDC will develop within the soft tissue of the incisive papilla. The typical diameter is 10&ndash;20&nbsp;mm, but they may reach several centimetres {1995816; 18587308; 25579059}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Radiology shows a corticated, symmetrical radiolucency in the anterior hard palate between the roots of the incisors, which may be displaced. Unless there are other reasons for loss of vitality, adjacent teeth are vital with intact lamina dura. Radiographic superimposition of the anterior nasal spine often produces a characteristic heart- or pear-shaped radiolucency in occlusal view. Diagnosis requires a size of &gt;&nbsp;6&nbsp;mm (the diameter of the normal incisive canal {1995816}), slightly more in older patients {31640721}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114291,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fewer than 5% of all cysts of the jaws are NDCs, but they account for as many as 80% of all non-odontogenic cysts {8170660; 16827841}. NDC occurs most frequently in patients aged 30&ndash;60&nbsp;years, with an M:F&nbsp;ratio of about 3:1 {29248496}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114292,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>NDC is categorized as a developmental cyst and arises from respiratory and squamous epithelial vestigial remnants of an embryonic nasopalatine duct present in some individuals {27860365}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114293,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In one&nbsp;third of cases, inflammation from non-vital teeth or periodontal ligament may be a factor, by stimulating the epithelial remnants to proliferate {18587308; 25579059}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114294,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibrous curettings and cyst lining</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114295,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>About 90% of NDCs are lined by non-keratinized stratified squamous epithelium, with focal cuboidal, columnar, or ciliated areas. About half contain respiratory epithelium, but &lt;&nbsp;10% are lined entirely by it {1995816; 29248496}. Cysts with respiratory-type epithelium tend to be more superiorly placed in the incisive canal {18587308}. The cyst wall contains prominent neurovascular bundles and occasionally mucous glands or cartilage.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114296,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears of aspirated cysts show degenerative cyst fluid with debris and macrophages, some of which contain haemosiderin. Epithelium is absent or scant. However, these findings are nonspecific.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114297,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114298,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> epicentre in the incisive canal; lining of non-keratinized squamous or respiratory epithelium.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> a neurovascular bundle in the cyst wall.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114299,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114300,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 132,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>NDCs do not normally recur after enucleation.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:16:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]